      "version": 1,
      "summary": "Fixed the lint failure in the sample todo seed: destructuring the repository method off the seed context tripped @typescript-eslint/unbound-method. The seed now calls repository on the context, and a new logic test covers the seed's three states and its idempotent re-run.",
      "blockers": [],
      "issues": [
        {
          "phase": "lint",
          "title": "unbound-method error in 202610070002_sample_todos.ts",
          "symptom": "eslint failed with @typescript-eslint/unbound-method at the seed's run({ repository }) parameter.",
          "rootCause": "SeedContext.repository is a method without a `this: void` annotation, so destructuring it from the context creates an unbound method reference.",
          "resolution": "Changed the seed to take the full context and call context.repository('todo'), keeping the method bound to its object.",
          "status": "resolved"
        }
      ],
      "improvements": [
        {
          "category": "verification",
          "title": "Seed definitions had no test coverage",
          "detail": "The failing seed was the only file without a matching test, so a lint-only defect was the first signal it produced.",
          "suggestedChange": "When adding a seed, add a logic test that runs it against a stub repository and asserts the created rows and repeat-run idempotency.",
          "mechanizable": false
        }
      ]
